<span id="Overview"></span>
== Übersicht ==

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
This page is a cheat sheet for the OpenCASCADE Draw tool.  Important links:
* [[#Cheat_sheet|The cheat sheet]]
* The [https://dev.opencascade.org/doc/overview/html/occt_user_guides__test_harness.html OpenCASCADE Draw user guide]
* [[#Background_information|Background information]]
</div>

<span id="Cheat_sheet"></span>
=== Spickzettel ===

<span id="Initialization"></span>
==== Initialisierung ====

Alle Module laden:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
pload ALL
}}

Eine Draw/tcl-Datei (zum Beispiel {{Incode|test.tcl}}) laden:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
source test.tcl
}}

Dateien auf dem System suchen:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
pwd
cd ..
ls
}}

<span id="Restore_a_BREP_file"></span>
==== Eine BREP-Datei wiederherstellen ====

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Restore file {{Incode|model.test}} into variable {{Incode|model}}:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
restore model.test model
}}

<span id="Display_a_model"></span>
==== Ein Modell anzeigen ====

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Display model {{Incode|model}}:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
vdisplay model
vfit
}}

<span id="Find_an_edge_or_face_in_the_model"></span>
==== Eine Kante oder Fläche im Modell finden ====

Zuerst das Modell anzeigen.

Für Kanten den Auswahlmodus 2, für Flächen den Auswahlmodus 4 wählen:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
vselmod 2 on
}}

Eine Kante oder Fläche im Fenster auswählen und die Nummer der Kante oder Fläche finden:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
vstate
}}

Darin wird in etwa Folgendes stehen:

{{Code|code=
Locally selected sub-shapes within model:
       Edge #4
}}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Explode model {{Incode|model}} with {{Incode|e}} for edges or {{Incode|f}} for faces:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
explode model e
}}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
You can access edge #4 with {{Incode|model_4}}, for example displaying it:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
vdisplay model_4
}}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Get a subshape of a model {{Incode|model}} directly, face 3 and display it:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
subshape model f 3
vdisplay model_3
}}

<span id="Checking_shapes"></span>
==== Formen überprüfen ====

Verschiedene Befehle zur Überprüfung der Form {{Incode|shape}}:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
checkshape shape
bopcheck shape
whatis shape
nbshapes shape
}}

<span id="Tolerances"></span>
==== Toleranzen ====

Die Formtoleranzen einer Form {{Incode|shape}} überprüfen:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
toler shape
dump shape
}}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Set the tolerance of a shape {{Incode|shape}}:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
dset tolerance 0.0001
settolerance shape tolerance
}}

<span id="Fillets_and_chamfers"></span>
==== Verrundungen und Fasen ====

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Create a fillet with radius 0.5 or a chamfer with distance 0.5 on the first edge of {{Incode|model}} and store it in shape {{Incode|result}}.  Notice that the position of the radius and distance is reversed for the two different calls, for fillet:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
blend result model 0.5 model_1
}}

Für Fasen:

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
chamf result model model_1 0.5
}}

<span id="Create_a_box"></span>
==== Einen Quader erstellen ====

Erstelle ein Quader {{Incode|b}}

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
box b 0 0 0 1 2 3
}}

<span id="Background_information"></span>
=== Hintergrundinformationen ===

==== Installation ====

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The Draw program is typically installed together with your OpenCASCADE distribution.  On Linux, you can typically find the program in your path under {{Incode|DRAWEXE}}.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
If you followed [[Compile_with_OCCT|Compile with OCCT]], you can find the Draw tool of the custom version in your distribution directory, in the {{Incode|bin}} directory of your distribution.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
To make sure that I load an OCCT Draw from a particular distribution, I have the following function in my {{Incode|$HOME/.bashrc}}:
</div>

{{Code|lang=tcl|code=
function set-occt() {
    if [ -z "$1" ]; then
	echo "Usage: set-occt <dir>"
	return 1
    fi
    if [ ! -d "$1" ]; then
	echo "Error: Directory $1 does not exist"
	return 1
    fi
    pushd "$1" > /dev/null
    export CASROOT=
    export CSF_OCCTResourcePath=$PWD/share/opencascade/resources
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$PWD/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
    export PATH=$PWD/bin:$PATH
    source ./bin/env.sh
    popd > /dev/null
}
}}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Suppose I want to make use of the OCCT version that is in the following installation directory {{Incode|/scratch/dist-occt-main}}, I execute the following in my bash shell:
</div>

{{Code|lang=bash|code=
set-occt /scratch/dist-occt-main
}}

Ich überprüfe, ob sich das richtige Draw-Programm tatsächlich in meinem Pfad befindet:

{{Code|lang=bash|code=
which DRAWEXE
}}

Das sollte Folgendes ausgeben:

{{Code||code=
/scratch/dist-occt-main/bin/DRAWEXE
}}

Die Versionsnummer kann wie folgt überprüft werden:

{{Code|lang=bash|code=
DRAWEXE --help
}}


